  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They didn't fold down six. Serven and Muncy made sure of that.",
    "what_this_means": "Late-inning rallies work until they don't. They scored nothing in the first four innings, left runners stranded twice in critical spots, then woke up in the fifth and scored six. That's the pattern this team has leaned on. Sleep early, explode when it matters, trust the pen to hold. It worked here. Muncy's go-ahead shot in the seventh broke a tie that shouldn't have been close. But nine hits and 16 strikeouts in one game is a strange kind of offense. They're winning on exactly the moments they convert, which means every game is a coin flip with good luck attached. Three straight one-run wins. That math gets harder.",
    "what_to_watch": "Zebby Matthews takes the ball for Minnesota tonight at 6:40 PM PT with a 5.12 ERA. The kind of matchup where early silence could become fatal if the pen isn't sharp again.",
